        "original_id": "b1243bfd-89ba-5ccf-9889-3f44338a463d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steven Weinberg, Sheldon Lee Glashow, Abdus Salam, Jogesh Pati\n- Roles: theoretical physicist, Nobel laureate, professor, board member\n- Organizations: Boston University, Harvard University, Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists\n- Concepts: electroweak unification, asymptotic safety, quantum gravity, UV completion, preon\n\nFacts:\n- Steven Weinberg was born on May 3, 1933.\n- In 1974, Jogesh Pati and Abdus Salam coined the word \"preon.\"\n- Steven Weinberg is an American theoretical physicist and a Nobel laureate in Physics.\n- Steven Weinberg, Abdus Salam, and Sheldon Glashow received recognition for contributions to the unification of the weak force and electromagnetic interaction between elementary particles.\n- Sheldon Lee Glashow is the Metcalf Professor of Mathematics and Physics at Boston University.\n- Sheldon Lee Glashow is Higgins Professor of Physics, Emeritus, at Harvard University.\n- Sheldon Lee Glashow is a member of the Board of Sponsors for the Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists.\n- Steven Weinberg originally proposed asymptotic safety to find a theory of quantum gravity.\n- The idea of a nontrivial fixed point as a possible UV completion can also be applied to other field theories, especially perturbatively nonrenormalizable ones.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
